{
 "about": [
  "Timecode examples every implementation must pass (frames both ways, typed digits, refused timecodes). The master copy is this file, in the terminal-timecode package; Argento (core/display/timecode_examples.json, for its screens) and TerminalPlayer (tests/timecode_examples.json, for its mpv script) keep copies, and their tests fail if a copy differs.",
  "frames: a frame count from 00:00:00:00 and its timecode, both ways. fps is the real rate (23.976 counts as 24, 29.97 as 30). Drop-frame applies to 29.97 and 59.94 only; ';' before the frames. Values cross-checked against an independent implementation and known points (29.97 drop-frame: 17982 = 00:10:00;00, 107892 = 01:00:00;00).",
  "typed: eight typed digits and the timecode that exists at that rate (clamped; for drop-frame, a skipped number moves up to the first one that exists).",
  "refused: timecodes that don't exist at that rate, which a conversion must refuse rather than turn into a frame number: a number drop-frame skips, frames, seconds or minutes too high, 24 hours or more, a separator that doesn't match the drop-frame setting (';' means drop-frame), anything but two digits per field. Lenient forms people type or paste (1:0:0:0, 01000000) are the typing field's job, before conversion."
 ],
